---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { BRAND, LOCALES } from '../../config/brand.mjs';
export async function getStaticPaths(){ return LOCALES.map((lang)=>({params:{lang}})); }
const { lang } = Astro.params;
---
<BaseLayout lang={lang} path="about" title="About"
  description="What HANKUKIN is, who makes it, and how it is researched and written.">
  <div class="wrap policy">
    <h1>About HANKUKIN</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 13 August 2026</p>

    <p>HANKUKIN is an independent guide for people who found Korea through a drama, a film, a music
    video or a song, and want to know what is actually there. We start from the story — a scene, a
    place, a phrase — and follow it through to the practical end: how to get there, what it costs,
    what the words meant, and what you can buy from home if you cannot travel.</p>

    <h2>What we publish</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Scenes</strong> — filming locations and the places around them, with routes, costs and photo guidance.</li>
      <li><strong>Now</strong> — what is currently gaining attention in Korea, based on public data rather than guesswork.</li>
      <li><strong>Decode</strong> — Korean expressions and the tone, politeness and humour that subtitles cannot carry.</li>
      <li><strong>Culture &amp; History</strong> — the longer background behind the places and stories.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How this site is made</h2>
    <p>HANKUKIN is run by one person. Research, drafting, translation, link checking and fact
    verification are carried out with AI assistance under a written
    <a href={`/${lang}/editorial-policy`}>editorial policy</a>. That policy decides what may be
    stated as fact, what must be softened, and what is discarded outright — and it is applied by the
    system before anything is published, not afterwards.</p>
    <p>We think you should be told this plainly rather than discover it. Every article carries its
    sources and the date it was last verified. If something is wrong, we would rather take the page
    down and re-check it than leave it up.</p>

    <h2>What we will not do</h2>
    <p>We do not publish where artists live, who they are seeing, where they were spotted, or which
    restaurant they supposedly frequent. We do not reproduce drama stills or celebrity photographs
    whose rights are unclear. We do not claim an artist uses a product unless there is an official
    source saying so. These are not editorial preferences — they are rules the publishing system
    enforces.</p>

    <h2>Independence</h2>
    <p>HANKUKIN is not affiliated with any broadcaster, production company, agency, artist, tourism
    authority or local government. Where we earn commission, we say so on the page. See our
    <a href={`/${lang}/affiliate-disclosure`}>affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>{BRAND.supportEmail} — or use the <a href={`/${lang}/contact`}>contact page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
